PHASE 1 — CODE DISCOVERY (Sourcegraph)
Run ALL lockfile query families for EACH vulnerable version/range bucket, always using regex form /.../ and context:global, scoped to org repos:
(context:global (repo:^github.com/<org1>/ OR repo:^github.com/<org2>/ OR ...))

A) Yarn classic:
file:yarn.lock$ /\/<PACKAGE_NAME_ESCAPED>\/-\/<PACKAGE_BASENAME_ESCAPED>-<VERSION_REGEX>\./ count:500

B) Yarn berry:
file:yarn.lock$ /resolution: "<PACKAGE_NAME>@npm:<VERSION_REGEX>/ count:500

C) npm:
file:package-lock.json$ /"<PACKAGE_NAME>"\s*:\s*\{[^}]*"version":\s*"<VERSION_REGEX>/ count:500
file:package-lock.json$ /\/<PACKAGE_NAME_ESCAPED>\/-\/<PACKAGE_BASENAME_ESCAPED>-<VERSION_REGEX>\./ count:500

D) pnpm:
file:pnpm-lock.yaml$ /\/<PACKAGE_NAME>@<VERSION_REGEX>/ count:500

E) uv.lock:
file:uv.lock$ /name\s*=\s*"<PACKAGE_NAME>"/ /version\s*=\s*"<VERSION_REGEX>/ count:500
fallback:
file:uv.lock$ /name\s*=\s*"<PACKAGE_NAME>"/ count:500

F) Must include sub-folder lockfiles by using:
file:yarn.lock$, file:package-lock.json$, file:pnpm-lock.yaml$, file:uv.lock$

G) Boundary check:
Semver-compare and EXCLUDE boundary versions outside vulnerability scope; explicitly list exclusions.

H) Sanity checks (required):
file:(yarn.lock|package-lock.json|pnpm-lock.yaml)$ /[^@\w\-]<PACKAGE_NAME>[@\-]/ count:500
file:uv.lock$ /name\s*=\s*"<PACKAGE_NAME>"/ count:500
Verify broad presence repos >= flagged affected repos.

I) Global code reference sweep (required):
For each vulnerable version:
context:global (repo:^github.com/<org1>/ OR repo:^github.com/<org2>/ OR ...) /<PACKAGE_NAME>/ /<VERSION_REGEX>/ count:500
Classify evidence confidence:
- HIGH: lockfile/manifest pin
- MEDIUM: install command / CI / Dockerfile / dbt package pin
- LOW: docs/comments/changelog/ambiguous
LOW => mark “needs owner verification”, do not treat as confirmed exposure.

